<h2>The five questions to answer at the start of the year</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>How many clients can I serve well?</strong> Capacity ceiling. Not "how many can I sign" but "how many can I support without quality degrading".</li>
  <li><strong>What revenue do I want?</strong> Set a real number. Translate to monthly + lump-sum mix.</li>
  <li><strong>Where will the leads come from?</strong> Allocate target lead volume across channels: organic, outbound, network, paid, partner.</li>
  <li><strong>What is on the roadmap for the agency itself?</strong> Pages to ship, SOPs to write, samples to add, blog posts to publish.</li>
  <li><strong>What is the personal-life constraint?</strong> Family, health, travel. Hours per week the business gets, not "all of them".</li>
</ol>

